326	/// spec-6-5 — wraps the real `testWidgets` so every test in this file
327	/// automatically closes `sl<ChatCubit>()` right after its own body
328	/// completes (success or failure). A bootstrapped `ChatCubit` now always
329	/// starts a real `_insightInactivityTimer`; the ordinary `addTearDown`/
330	/// group-level `tearDown()` pattern this suite already uses for other
331	/// cleanup runs too late to satisfy `testWidgets`' own `!timersPending`
332	/// invariant check — that check runs *inside* the test's own callback
333	/// execution, before any `addTearDown`/`tearDown` callback ever fires.
334	/// Resolving the lazy singleton here is harmless even for a test that
335	/// never reaches `/` at all: resolving it alone never calls `init()`, so
336	/// no bootstrap/timer ever started in that case either.
337	void testWidgets(String description, WidgetTesterCallback callback) {
